> What?  Please explain/give example of this <movement> to which you refer...

If you are at the first line and first column of some text and want to
decode the complete text, then movement would be

   G

If you want to decode just to the end of the line, then movement would be

   $

So the complete commands to rot13 in vim would be

   g?G
   g?$

You can use other movements like until end of the word (e or E) to the end
of the paragraph, to the next matching bracket, etc.

